      <p>A broadcast studio is built to a commercial standard. You would expect to see this in a media company, a major brand's content team, or a high-profile public figure's home. It includes top-tier microphones, a professional broadcast mixer, full acoustic treatment on every wall, dedicated lighting rigs, multiple camera angles, and custom millwork or shelving for the set design. Most individual podcasters do not need this level. But for those building a media brand, it is the right investment.</p>

