      <p>The microphone is the single most impactful piece of equipment in any podcast setup, and the price range is enormous. At the low end, USB microphones like the Blue Yeti or Audio-Technica ATR2100x run $100 to $150. Mid-tier XLR microphones like the Shure SM7B or Rode PodMic run $200 to $450. At the professional end, broadcast-grade condenser microphones like the Neumann U87 or Shure SM7dB can run $800 to $3,000. For most professional setups, the $200 to $450 range hits a performance sweet spot that is hard to argue with.</p>

