      <p>Acoustic treatment is one of the highest-ROI investments in a home studio. Untreated rooms produce echo, flutter, and reverberation that no amount of post-processing can fully fix. A basic treatment package of foam panels or fiberglass acoustic panels costs $150 to $400 for a small room. A full room treatment with corner bass traps, wall panels, and ceiling clouds can run $600 to $2,000 depending on room size and panel quality. At ATL Podcast Pros, acoustic treatment is always included in our studio builds because it is the single biggest factor in audio quality after the microphone itself.</p>

