      <p>If you are recording video, the camera is a significant line item. A solid entry-level webcam like the Logitech Brio runs $200 to $250. A mirrorless camera like the Sony ZV-E10 or Canon M50 Mark II, used with a capture card, runs $600 to $1,200 for the camera alone. Add a capture card like the Elgato Cam Link at $130 and the lens if needed. Full video setups for multi-camera recording can run $2,000 to $6,000 when you include all cameras, capture cards, and switching equipment.</p>

